Base settings of WormOS for each hypervisor (worm vm). The file named
after the hypervisor found (qemu, kvm, virtualbox, vmware, hyperv, xen,
parallels, other, none) is read after the built-in defaults and before
/etc/worm/vm.conf, which `worm vm set KEY VALUE` writes. `auto` means
decided from what was found (the GPU, 3D acceleration). Keys:

  renderer   auto | gles | software
  cursor     auto | software | hardware
  scale      auto | 0.75 | 0.8 | 0.9 | 1 | 1.25 | 1.5 | 1.75 | 2
  clipboard  on | off      the SPICE agent (clip agent)
  agent      on | off      the guest agent
  shares     on | off      the host's shared folders under /media
  tuning     on | off      settings for virtual disks and memory
